[assistant] Here's a simple C# console application that fulfills your requirements:

```csharp
using System;

class GreetUserApp
{
    static void Main()
    {
        // Introduce the application
        Console.WriteLine("Welcome to the Greet User App!");
        Console.WriteLine("This application will greet you by your name.\n");

        // Request user's name
        Console.Write("Please enter your name: ");
        string userName = Console.ReadLine();

        // Say hello to the user
        Console.WriteLine($"\nHello, {userName}! Nice to meet you.");

        // Wait for user input before closing the console window
        Console.Write("\nPress any key to exit...");
        Console.ReadKey();
    }
}
```

To run this application, save it as `GreetUserApp.cs` and then use the `dotnet run` command if you're using the .NET Core CLI, or press F5 if you're using Visual Studio or Visual Studio Code with the C# extension.
